            "body": "@WingDust  What exactly do you mean by `level`? Could you explain a bit more?  \r\n\r\nIf you're referring to the [mini.indentscope](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ee23e1abc206efc6d6cce19ec8c0a3da7a897035/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L68-L72) link, it mentions how to disable it globally (`vim.g.miniindentscope_disable`) or for a specific buffer (`vim.b.miniindentscope_disable`).  \r\n\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/WingDust/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/WingDust\">@WingDust</a>  What exactly do you mean by <code class=\"notranslate\">level</code>? Could you explain a bit more?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you're referring to the <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ee23e1abc206efc6d6cce19ec8c0a3da7a897035/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L68-L72\">mini.indentscope</a> link, it mentions how to disable it globally (<code class=\"notranslate\">vim.g.miniindentscope_disable</code>) or for a specific buffer (<code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.miniindentscope_disable</code>).</p>",
