        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There is [`config.draw.predicate`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ee23e1abc206efc6d6cce19ec8c0a3da7a897035/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L136-L138) specifically for this. The input has [scope structure](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ee23e1abc206efc6d6cce19ec8c0a3da7a897035/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L290-L300).\r\n\r\nNot drawing indent line at the first column can be done something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal draw_big_level = function(scope) return scope.border.indent > 1 end\r\nrequire('mini.indentscope').setup({ draw = { predicate = draw_big_level } })\r\n```\r\n\r\nFine-tuning this to fit the concept of \"levels\" (which probably depends on 'shiftwidth', 'tabstop', and maybe other options) is left to the user.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">There is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ee23e1abc206efc6d6cce19ec8c0a3da7a897035/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L136-L138\"><code class=\"notranslate\">config.draw.predicate</code></a> specifically for this. The input has <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ee23e1abc206efc6d6cce19ec8c0a3da7a897035/doc/mini-indentscope.txt#L290-L300\">scope structure</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not drawing indent line at the first column can be done something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local draw_big_level = function(scope) return scope.border.indent &gt; 1 end\nrequire('mini.indentscope').setup({ draw = { predicate = draw_big_level } })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">draw_big_level</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">scope</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">scope</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">border</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">indent</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.indentscope<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({ <span class=\"pl-smi\">draw</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">predicate</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">draw_big_level</span> } })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fine-tuning this to fit the concept of \"levels\" (which probably depends on 'shiftwidth', 'tabstop', and maybe other options) is left to the user.</p>",
            "bodyText": "There is config.draw.predicate specifically for this. The input has scope structure.\nNot drawing indent line at the first column can be done something like this:\nlocal draw_big_level = function(scope) return scope.border.indent > 1 end\nrequire('mini.indentscope').setup({ draw = { predicate = draw_big_level } })\nFine-tuning this to fit the concept of \"levels\" (which probably depends on 'shiftwidth', 'tabstop', and maybe other options) is left to the user.",
